{
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## Step 7: compare with the model answers\nFor each question, read your answer and the model answer, and say whether yours says the same.",
      "id": "class_s01_compare_0"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**Checkpoint 2.** What identifies a process for the engine?\n\n*Yours:* {{checkpoint2}}\n\n*Model:* The process id. The name is only a label: the same id with another name is a new version of the same process; another id is a different process.",
      "id": "class_s01_compare_1"
    },
    {
      "type": "radio",
      "key": "rateCheckpoint2",
      "label": "Does yours say the same?",
      "values": [
        {
          "label": "Yes, it says the same",
          "value": "yes"
        },
        {
          "label": "Partly",
          "value": "partly"
        },
        {
          "label": "No, I missed it",
          "value": "no"
        }
      ],
      "validate": {
        "required": true
      },
      "id": "class_s01_compare_2"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**Drawing vs executable model.**\n\n*Yours:* {{self1}}\n\n*Model:* An executable model is marked executable; its tasks have a type the engine runs (user task, service task...) instead of abstract tasks; its gateways read variables (conditions or a default flow); its start events say how an instance starts. The drawing only has to be understood by people.",
      "id": "class_s01_compare_3"
    },
    {
      "type": "radio",
      "key": "rateSelf1",
      "label": "Does yours say the same?",
      "values": [
        {
          "label": "Yes, it says the same",
          "value": "yes"
        },
        {
          "label": "Partly",
          "value": "partly"
        },
        {
          "label": "No, I missed it",
          "value": "no"
        }
      ],
      "validate": {
        "required": true
      },
      "id": "class_s01_compare_4"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**Instance and version.**\n\n*Yours:* {{self2}}\n\n*Model:* An instance is one run of a deployed process, with its own token and variables. A version is one deployment of the model with the same id; every instance keeps the version it started with.",
      "id": "class_s01_compare_5"
    },
    {
      "type": "radio",
      "key": "rateSelf2",
      "label": "Does yours say the same?",
      "values": [
        {
          "label": "Yes, it says the same",
          "value": "yes"
        },
        {
          "label": "Partly",
          "value": "partly"
        },
        {
          "label": "No, I missed it",
          "value": "no"
        }
      ],
      "validate": {
        "required": true
      },
      "id": "class_s01_compare_6"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**\"Nothing happens.\"**\n\n*Yours:* {{self3}}\n\n*Model:* Operate: find the instance and see where the token is. Usually it waits in a user task (then it is in Tasklist) or it stopped at an incident.",
      "id": "class_s01_compare_7"
    },
    {
      "type": "radio",
      "key": "rateSelf3",
      "label": "Does yours say the same?",
      "values": [
        {
          "label": "Yes, it says the same",
          "value": "yes"
        },
        {
          "label": "Partly",
          "value": "partly"
        },
        {
          "label": "No, I missed it",
          "value": "no"
        }
      ],
      "validate": {
        "required": true
      },
      "id": "class_s01_compare_8"
    }
  ],
  "type": "default",
  "id": "class-s01-compare",
  "executionPlatform": "Camunda Cloud",
  "executionPlatformVersion": "8.9.0",
  "schemaVersion": 18
}
